Make nix-provided Python the only interpreter source by default.

uv ships `python-preference = managed`, which prefers its own prebuilt
CPython in a machine-global cache (~/.local/share/uv/python). Making those
work under nix means patchelf-ing them in place, mutating state shared with
every other project on the host. uv-nix resolves interpreters from nix
instead (see the hook in 03-uv-python-nix-hook.patch), so uv itself must
never select or download one.

User overrides (--python-preference, UV_PYTHON_PREFERENCE, uv.toml) still
win: settings.rs resolves them via unwrap_or_default().

diff --git a/crates/uv-python/src/discovery.rs b/crates/uv-python/src/discovery.rs
index 1a027b2..7f06239 100644
--- a/crates/uv-python/src/discovery.rs
+++ b/crates/uv-python/src/discovery.rs
@@ -114,7 +114,6 @@ impl serde::Serialize for PythonRequest {
 pub enum PythonPreference {
     /// Only use managed Python installations; never use system Python installations.
     OnlyManaged,
-    #[default]
     /// Prefer managed Python installations over system Python installations.
     ///
     /// System Python installations are still preferred over downloading managed Python versions.
@@ -124,6 +123,7 @@ pub enum PythonPreference {
     ///
     /// If a system Python installation cannot be found, a managed Python installation can be used.
     System,
+    #[default]
     /// Only use system Python installations; never use managed Python installations.
     OnlySystem,
 }
